&lt;p&gt;The Snr. Renewal Specialist Director (EMEA) oversees the renewals department for EMEA, managing global team members and processes for all KnowBe4 and Egress customers within EMEA. They ensure timely renewals and maintain retention rates. Acting as a knowledge base and escalation point for commercial, contractual, and process issues, churn reviews and forecasts, providing insights to senior leadership. They guide Renewal Specialists, create best practices, and deliver training across teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the EMEA renewals team, including Global team members, book of business, reporting, and processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive processes for Renewal Specialist teams to coordinate with CSMs to strategize on renewals and applicable upsells for their customers to maximize bookings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pricing strategies that meet the Company’s standards, policies, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required to work with the global sales team and channel network to ensure we are quoting renewals on time and retaining existing business, managing the 90-day renewals pipeline, and maintaining a company-set target retention rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependable knowledge base and point of escalation for all topics Commercial, Contractual, or Process relating to Retaining and Renewing Customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in regular Churn QBRs, Forecasts, and talks with SVP Global Renewals and customer-facing teams to deliver insights on Product churn, highlighting potential customer/market trends to develop business strategies and improve product development and CS enablement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required to create and own best practices within Renewals and deliver enablement to Renewals, Account Services, Channel, Legal, and Finance teams, with a specialty in delivering CPQ/Licensing training. CPQ, Licensing, Cloud Framework, and MSA Specialist.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend Customer Account Reviews/Health checks alongside Account Services as the expert on Renewal commercials, Risk Mitigation, and Contract Negotiations when required, with a specialty in Enterprise Business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for creating and improving company Dashboards and Reports on all topics of Retention, Risk, and Renewals Pipeline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage weekly pipeline reviews with Renewal Specialists and meet regularly with SVP Global Renewals to strategize and review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline and enhance existing CRM processes to improve Renewals&#39; best practices and support Sales Operations and Enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and groom a high performing Renewal Specialist team and successfully manage the daily, weekly, monthly and quarterly production to meet and exceed targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage Personal Success Plans for Renewal Specialists that are underperforming and need improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authority to hire or fire subordinate employees makes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authority to hire or fire subordinate employees, or the Snr. Renewal Specialist Director (EMEA) makes suggestions and recommendations as to the hiring, firing, advancement, promotion or any other change of status of subordinate employees that are given particular weight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
