&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are the UK&#39;s leading premium publisher, home to iconic and influential media brands including Esquire, Men&#39;s &amp;amp; Women&#39;s Health, ELLE, Good Housekeeping, Harper&#39;s Bazaar, Digital Spy, Cosmopolitan, Red and more. At Hearst UK, we don&#39;t just create content – we shape culture.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our workplace is driven by passion, shaped by authenticity and powered by creativity. We back bold ideas, act with an entrepreneurial mindset and continually evolve to meet the moment – while respecting the legacy that&#39;s brought us here. We believe in each other&#39;s potential and push boundaries together to create meaningful impact, both across the media landscape and in people&#39;s lives.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We&#39;re proud of our heritage – but even more excited about making history.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Hearst UK operates an in-office policy with flexible Fridays. Our office is based at &lt;strong&gt;House of Hearst, 30 Panton Street, St James&#39;s, London, SW1Y 4AJ&lt;/strong&gt;, where teams collaborate in person and connect across brands and functions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary - £55,000 - £65,000 + 40% Commision - &lt;/strong&gt;Salary is dependent on experience and will be assessed in line with the candidate&#39;s skills, knowledge and relevant expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role...&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Director, you will be responsible for growing and managing a portfolio of key client and agency relationships across Hearst UK, combining strong commercial thinking with a deep understanding of our brands, audiences and advertising solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own your accounts from strategy through to delivery, developing trusted relationships with senior agency and client stakeholders and identifying opportunities to grow revenue across Hearst’s full portfolio. Working across print, digital, social, data, programmatic, content partnerships and events, you will bring together the right Hearst solutions to meet client objectives and create long-term commercial value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly relationship-led and commercially focused role. You will work closely with the wider sales, creative strategy, marketing and operations teams to develop compelling responses to briefs, turn insight into opportunities and ensure clients receive a consistently high level of service. You will also act as a senior representative for Hearst across the industry, helping to strengthen our reputation and relationships across your agency and client network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Duties…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow a portfolio of key client and agency accounts, developing strategic plans that deliver against revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with senior stakeholders across client, planning, investment, digital and buying teams, ensuring Hearst is front-of-mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and convert new business and growth opportunities across Hearst’s full commercial portfolio, from existing spenders through to new prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong understanding of each client’s business, objectives, category and media strategy, using insight to shape relevant commercial opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales, creative strategy, content, marketing, digital and operations teams to develop integrated, high-quality responses to briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted consultant to clients and agencies, confidently presenting Hearst’s capabilities, products, audience insight and market opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial conversations and negotiations, ensuring proposals are strategically strong, commercially viable and delivered to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development of client presentations, proposals, case studies and market insight, ensuring a consistent and compelling Hearst story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong pipeline of opportunities and ensure account activity, forecasting and revenue information are accurate and up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Hearst at industry events, meetings and client entertainment, building the external profile and network of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share client, agency and industry insight internally, helping the wider team identify trends, opportunities and changing market needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an ambassador for Hearst UK, its brands and values, delivering best-in-class service and strengthening long-term partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a senior commercial, agency sales, media or client partnership role, with a strong track record of growing revenue and accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the media and advertising landscape, with experience across both digital and traditional channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to develop strategic account plans and turn client insight into tangible commercial opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exceptional relationship builder with established agency and/or client contacts and the confidence to build relationships at senior level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and negotiation skills, with a clear focus on revenue, results and long-term account growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the confidence to influence senior internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across multiple teams and disciplines, bringing together creative, commercial and operational expertise to deliver the right solution for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organised and commercially driven, able to manage multiple priorities while maintaining a high standard of client service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, curious and solutions-focused approach, with the ability to spot opportunities, challenge thinking and connect the dots across the Hearst portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong team player who contributes to a positive, collaborative and high-performance culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(Your benefits at Hearst UK are more than just extras—they are tools to help you thrive in every part of life.)&lt;/p&gt;
